00:34:52.091 --> 00:34:54.221
Yeah. yeah. Yeah. I can feel it.

516
00:34:54.427 --> 00:34:55.507
- He's growing.
- Wow.

517
00:34:55.678 --> 00:34:58.508
Changing every day.

518
00:35:00.349 --> 00:35:01.929
- Heh.
- Mm.

519
00:35:08.983 --> 00:35:11.863
Can I admit something to you?

520
00:35:13.529 --> 00:35:16.909
It's a little weird that
I'm pregnant with your baby.

521
00:35:18.201 --> 00:35:21.251
That you're inside of me...

522
00:35:21.412 --> 00:35:23.162
- ...in that way.
- Mm.

523
00:35:23.331 --> 00:35:26.291
Yeah. yeah. that is strange. isn't it?

524
00:35:26.918 --> 00:35:28.128
Yeah.

525
00:35:28.294 --> 00:35:30.134
But we're grateful for that.

526
00:35:30.296 --> 00:35:33.716
Because without you.
we couldn't do any of this.

527
00:35:33.883 --> 00:35:35.843
I like it.

528
00:35:39.388 --> 00:35:41.598
- Mm.
- Yep.

529
00:35:43.559 --> 00:35:46.099
Hey. listen. next week we're
having our annual charity event...

530
00:35:46.270 --> 00:35:47.810
...here at the house. You should join us.

531
00:35:47.980 --> 00:35:49.690
- What's it for?
- We like to raise money...

532
00:35:49.857 --> 00:35:52.527
...for the Boys and Girls Club of America.

533
00:35:52.819 --> 00:35:56.239
You're amazing. Yes. I will come.

534
00:35:56.447 --> 00:35:58.367
[♪♪♪]

535
00:36:15.633 --> 00:36:17.593
What's so important?

536
00:36:20.096 --> 00:36:22.096
[♪♪♪]

537
00:36:22.598 --> 00:36:24.598
Good to see you too.

538
00:36:24.767 --> 00:36:26.597
I missed you. baby.

539
00:36:26.769 --> 00:36:29.269
I'm so glad you miss me.

540
00:36:30.815 --> 00:36:32.185
You look nice.

541
00:36:33.609 --> 00:36:38.609
I mean. living up there in that beautiful
big house. that must be nice.

542
00:36:38.781 --> 00:36:42.121
Did you know that you have
their only embryo?

543
00:36:42.285 --> 00:36:46.325
- It's a baby now.
- And they don't have any more.

544
00:36:46.831 --> 00:36:48.711
And in the eyes of the law...

545
00:36:48.875 --> 00:36:52.545
...since it's inside of you.
it belongs to us.

546
00:36:53.379 --> 00:36:57.969
We can decide to keep it for ourselves
anytime we want.

547
00:36:58.134 --> 00:37:01.304
- But I... I thought...
- Don't think.

548
00:37:01.679 --> 00:37:03.889
It's not your thing. baby.

549
00:37:04.056 --> 00:37:06.226
I'm the brains on this.

550
00:37:06.684 --> 00:37:08.944
You're just the uterus.

551
00:37:16.193 --> 00:37:18.403
So here's what you're gonna do.

552
00:37:18.571 --> 00:37:21.991
Every single month. you're gonna say...

553
00:37:22.158 --> 00:37:25.698
...that you're changing your mind.
and you're keeping it.

554
00:37:25.870 --> 00:37:27.620
And they'll pay.

555
00:37:27.788 --> 00:37:29.958
Maybe four grand. maybe more.

556
00:37:30.124 --> 00:37:31.834
Mike.

557
00:37:33.252 --> 00:37:36.342
- They've been really good to me.
- Mm.

558
00:37:37.214 --> 00:37:40.384
John really wants to be a father.

559
00:37:46.849 --> 00:37:48.639
Does he?

560
00:37:49.685 --> 00:37:51.685
Does he really?

561
00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:55.860
Hmm...

562
00:38:18.506 --> 00:38:20.586
You're into him.

563
00:38:22.301 --> 00:38:26.181
What do you think is gonna happen. Anna?

564
00:38:26.764 --> 00:38:28.394
Hm?

565
00:38:29.308 --> 00:38:33.268
You'll live happily ever after
with him in that big house?

566
00:38:34.772 --> 00:38:36.232
Hm?

567
00:38:36.399 --> 00:38:38.609
He doesn't care about you.

568
00:38:38.985 --> 00:38:41.735
You are like a cow to him.

569
00:38:41.904 --> 00:38:43.954
Ow. Ow.

570
00:38:44.115 --> 00:38:47.615
Unh. I'll do it.
I'll do it. Mike. I'll do it.

571
00:38:48.244 --> 00:38:50.124
I know you will.

572
00:38:50.287 --> 00:38:52.497
I'll do it. I'll tell them.

573
00:38:58.671 --> 00:39:01.261
I'll do it for you. baby.

574
00:39:02.425 --> 00:39:05.135
- Anything you want.
- Mm.

575
00:39:05.636 --> 00:39:08.636
MAN: ♪ Well. if I don't love you. baby ♪

576
00:39:08.806 --> 00:39:10.636
♪ Grits ain't groceries ♪

577
00:39:10.808 --> 00:39:12.268
♪ Eggs ain't poultry ♪

578
00:39:12.476 --> 00:39:16.936
♪ And Mona Lisa was a man ♪

579
00:39:17.106 --> 00:39:18.766
[BAND PLAYING UPBEAT BLUES MUSIC]

580
00:39:19.900 --> 00:39:24.700
It's from the firm. And tell Laura
she absolutely tops herself...

581
00:39:24.864 --> 00:39:27.374
- ...every time you guys do this.
- I'll do that. Thanks.

582
00:39:27.533 --> 00:39:30.583
Nobody knows this yet.
but Grafton Industries...

583
00:39:30.745 --> 00:39:34.535
...is unofficially
floating settlement offers.

584
00:39:34.707 --> 00:39:37.417
- You're not gonna settle with them?
- You kidding me?

585
00:39:37.585 --> 00:39:40.125
All this time. you've been telling me
we had them by the balls.

586
00:39:40.296 --> 00:39:42.166
I just wasn't sure.

587
00:39:42.339 --> 00:39:43.719
But now I am.

588
00:39:44.508 --> 00:39:47.298
This is gonna lock up partner
for you. John.

589
00:39:47.470 --> 00:39:49.010
You take them to trial.

590
00:39:49.180 --> 00:39:50.560
Gut them like a fish.

591
00:39:50.973 --> 00:39:52.733
I'll do that.

592
00:39:52.933 --> 00:39:54.693
♪ Grits ain't groceries ♪

593
00:39:54.852 --> 00:39:56.312
♪ Eggs ain't poultry ♪

594
00:39:56.520 --> 00:40:00.940
♪ And Mona Lisa was a man ♪♪

595
00:40:01.650 --> 00:40:02.740
Aw...

596
00:40:02.943 --> 00:40:04.493
Look. I was talking to Anna earlier.

597
00:40:04.653 --> 00:40:06.953
I didn't realise she was
your second cousin. man.

598
00:40:07.114 --> 00:40:08.994
- She is amazing.
- Todd. she's 21.

599
00:40:09.575 --> 00:40:11.735
My calculation. that's...

600
00:40:11.911 --> 00:40:14.001
That's legal plus three. right?

601
00:40:14.747 --> 00:40:17.787
I'm just checking with you. You wouldn't
mind if I asked her out. would you?

602
00:40:17.958 --> 00:40:19.498
No. You can ask her out.

603
00:40:19.668 --> 00:40:22.588
[CROWD APPLAUDING AND GLASS CLINKING]

604
00:40:24.340 --> 00:40:26.130
Normally. this is the part
of the evening...

605
00:40:26.300 --> 00:40:28.930
...where John asks all of you
to reach for your chequebooks.

606
00:40:29.762 --> 00:40:33.102
And I'm sure he'll manage
to get that in still...

607
00:40:33.724 --> 00:40:35.524
...but first. I wanted everyone to know...

608
00:40:35.684 --> 00:40:40.314
...how important the Boys and Girls
Clubs of America is to us.

609
00:40:40.481 --> 00:40:42.691
Especially to my husband.

610
00:40:42.858 --> 00:40:46.068
John loves children. and they love him.

611
00:40:46.278 --> 00:40:48.278
Thank you. John.

612
00:40:49.573 --> 00:40:51.623
I'd also like...

613
00:40:51.909 --> 00:40:53.909
[♪♪♪]

614
00:40:55.996 --> 00:40:59.706
I'd also like to thank all of you here...

615
00:40:59.875 --> 00:41:01.745
...for coming tonight and. um...

616
00:41:01.919 --> 00:41:03.799
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

617
00:41:03.963 --> 00:41:05.513
[MOUTHING] Thank you.

618
00:41:05.714 --> 00:41:07.264
Thank you.

619
00:41:09.093 --> 00:41:10.683
Now you can all take out your chequebooks.

620
00:41:10.845 --> 00:41:12.715
[CROWD LAUGHS THEN APPLAUDING]

621
00:41:16.058 --> 00:41:18.058
Is that the dress you gave her?

622
00:41:18.227 --> 00:41:20.097
No. It's not.

623
00:41:20.271 --> 00:41:22.231
You want me to go talk to her?

624
00:41:22.398 --> 00:41:25.068
No. I will.

625
00:41:25.234 --> 00:41:26.994
[BAND PLAYING UPBEAT JAZZ MUSIC]

626
00:41:27.153 --> 00:41:29.113
[CHATTERING]

627
00:41:29.280 --> 00:41:30.700
Excuse me. gentlemen.

628
00:41:32.283 --> 00:41:34.373
- Anna.
- What's the matter?

629
00:41:34.535 --> 00:41:35.945
That's not the dress I gave you.

630
00:41:36.871 --> 00:41:38.331
Oh.

631
00:41:38.497 --> 00:41:40.537
God. I'm so sorry.

632
00:41:40.708 --> 00:41:43.338
It's just. the one that
you gave me didn't really fit.

633
00:41:44.128 --> 00:41:48.378
I was gonna ask you.
but you were so busy with the party.

634
00:41:49.633 --> 00:41:51.763
I can... I can go change...

635
00:41:51.927 --> 00:41:55.177
- ...right now.
- No. it's fine.

636
00:41:56.015 --> 00:41:57.925
You look great.

637
00:42:08.527 --> 00:42:10.397
Thank you for staying late.
I appreciate it.

638
00:42:10.571 --> 00:42:13.871
- Thank you. Thanks.
- Thank you.

639
00:42:14.033 --> 00:42:16.043
[R&B BALLAD PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

640
00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:23.040
♪ Broken hearts are made for two ♪

641
00:42:23.250 --> 00:42:26.420
♪ One for me and one for you ♪

642
00:42:26.587 --> 00:42:29.377
♪ Tell me. have you heard the news? ♪

643
00:42:29.632 --> 00:42:32.802
♪ We are now in love ♪

644
00:42:32.968 --> 00:42:36.058
♪ So I guess that I should mention ♪

645
00:42:36.222 --> 00:42:39.392
♪ That I am in no condition ♪

646
00:42:39.558 --> 00:42:42.518
♪ To put you in this position ♪

647
00:42:42.686 --> 00:42:45.226
♪ I might **** this up ♪

648
00:42:46.774 --> 00:42:49.324
Well. no one fell in the pool.

649
00:42:49.485 --> 00:42:50.895
The rain stayed away.

650
00:42:51.946 --> 00:42:54.106
I'd call that a win.

651
00:42:54.323 --> 00:42:56.333
I found it in your record collection.

652
00:43:00.579 --> 00:43:02.459
Where's Laura?

653
00:43:02.623 --> 00:43:05.043
Oh. yeah. she crashed about an hour ago.

654
00:43:05.251 --> 00:43:07.841
Has to catch a flight
at 6 in the morning for work.

655
00:43:08.003 --> 00:43:09.843
So how'd our little story hold up?

656
00:43:10.005 --> 00:43:11.835
[CHUCKLES]

657
00:43:12.007 --> 00:43:14.297
It was great.

658
00:43:14.468 --> 00:43:16.468
I was acting out a part.

659
00:43:17.263 --> 00:43:20.223
I had a secret in me that no one knew.

660
00:43:20.391 --> 00:43:21.891
♪ Don't go crazy ♪

661
00:43:22.059 --> 00:43:23.139
Except you.

662
00:43:23.727 --> 00:43:25.187
♪ For loving me ♪♪

663
00:43:25.354 --> 00:43:27.024
You know everybody loves you?

664
00:43:27.439 --> 00:43:30.399
- Shut up.
- I'm serious.

665
00:43:30.776 --> 00:43:34.196
It made me think that I made
a good choice for the baby.

666
00:43:35.739 --> 00:43:38.409
Well. I thought that we were
the ones that made the choice.

667
00:43:38.742 --> 00:43:40.202
I could've said no.

668
00:43:40.828 --> 00:43:42.198
True.

669
00:43:43.706 --> 00:43:45.826
You're gonna make a great dad.

670
00:43:47.459 --> 00:43:50.879
Well. I'm glad it was you.

671
00:43:58.721 --> 00:44:03.271
I am gonna take a bath before bed.

672
00:44:04.226 --> 00:44:05.976
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

673
00:44:09.106 --> 00:44:12.066
Thank you for everything. John.

674
00:44:27.458 --> 00:44:29.788
[THUMPING]

675
00:44:40.888 --> 00:44:42.848
[CREAKING AND THUMPING]

676
00:44:52.149 --> 00:44:53.649
Is everything okay?

677
00:44:54.109 --> 00:44:56.989
Something's knocking
against the guest house.

678
00:45:14.463 --> 00:45:16.473
[RATTLING]

679
00:45:17.925 --> 00:45:19.835
[♪♪♪]

680
00:46:09.268 --> 00:46:11.268
[♪♪♪]

681
00:46:30.914 --> 00:46:33.134
[DOOR OPENS]

682
00:46:42.593 --> 00:46:44.553
Is there coffee?

683
00:46:47.514 --> 00:46:48.684
Yeah. Coming right up.

684
00:46:50.058 --> 00:46:51.638
When does Laura get home?

685
00:46:51.852 --> 00:46:53.652
JOHN: Tuesday.

686
00:46:58.859 --> 00:47:00.859
So. look. about last night...

687
00:47:01.028 --> 00:47:02.448
Hm?

688
00:47:07.576 --> 00:47:09.196
Todd Decker. he was. uh...

689
00:47:09.369 --> 00:47:10.659
He was asking about you.

690
00:47:11.580 --> 00:47:15.920
The guy in the Grey suit? You know.
he was staring at me all night.

691
00:47:16.084 --> 00:47:17.844
Had to be uncomfortable for you.

692
00:47:18.795 --> 00:47:21.215
Can't blame a person for staring.

693
00:47:21.381 --> 00:47:24.221
It just means they like what they see.

694
00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:27.930
Actually. I prefer older guys.

695
00:47:28.096 --> 00:47:29.096
[PHONE RINGING]

696
00:47:29.264 --> 00:47:30.564
I always have.

697
00:47:30.724 --> 00:47:33.394
Mike was the youngest guy I ever dated.

698
00:47:33.560 --> 00:47:36.730
- Is that your phone?
- They'll leave a message.

699
00:47:38.398 --> 00:47:40.068
So I have to go into the office today.

700
00:47:40.234 --> 00:47:41.614
- On a Sunday?
- Yeah.

701
00:47:41.777 --> 00:47:44.567
I got an important deposition.
You can order out.

702
00:47:44.738 --> 00:47:46.158
I'm not gonna be back until late.

703
00:47:50.661 --> 00:47:53.121
[♪♪♪]

704
00:47:56.959 --> 00:47:59.629
How about we go out to the lake house?

705
00:47:59.795 --> 00:48:02.205
Just you and I. a weekend
before the baby comes.

706
00:48:02.381 --> 00:48:04.221
As soon as you get back from Houston.

707
00:48:04.383 --> 00:48:05.763
I'd like that.

708
00:48:05.926 --> 00:48:08.046
John. you're not gonna like this...

709
00:48:08.220 --> 00:48:10.430
...but Chef Folse wants me out here
tomorrow as well.

710
00:48:11.765 --> 00:48:14.725
- You're right. I don't like it.
- Should I say no?

711
00:48:15.269 --> 00:48:17.439
Should I just come home now?

712
00:48:18.021 --> 00:48:20.441
No. go ahead and stay. It's okay.

713
00:48:20.649 --> 00:48:22.569
[PHONE RINGING]

714
00:48:25.028 --> 00:48:28.118
- Hey.
- LAURA: I hope you're sitting down.

715
00:48:29.116 --> 00:48:32.866
Chef Folse is offering me
a major promotion.

716
00:48:33.036 --> 00:48:34.036
Really?

717
00:48:34.204 --> 00:48:36.584
That's the reason he brought me down.
so he could offer me...

718
00:48:36.748 --> 00:48:39.708
- ...the CEO position.
- Congratulations.

719
00:48:40.460 --> 00:48:42.090
[LAURA LAUGHS THEN JOHN CHUCKLES FLATLY]

720
00:48:42.254 --> 00:48:43.844
But I thought we talked about. you know...

721
00:48:44.006 --> 00:48:45.626
We have six months before the baby's born.

722
00:48:45.799 --> 00:48:49.049
I told him I could run the company while
we look for a permanent replacement.

723
00:48:49.219 --> 00:48:50.849
Why not just turn it down. sweetheart?

724
00:48:51.013 --> 00:48:53.893
I think I should take it.
even if it is only for six months.

725
00:48:54.099 --> 00:48:55.269
But that's assuming you agree.

726
00:48:55.434 --> 00:48:57.814
I mean. I'd have to spend
a few days a month up here.

727
00:48:57.978 --> 00:48:59.728
But that wouldn't be
until later in the year.

728
00:48:59.896 --> 00:49:01.566
And you could come up for some weekends.

729
00:49:02.399 --> 00:49:03.819
Babe. are you happy for me?

730
00:49:03.984 --> 00:49:07.204
- I really wanna do this.
- Yeah. no. sweetheart. Definitely.

731
00:49:07.362 --> 00:49:09.532
I'm. uh... I'm definitely happy for you.

732
00:49:09.740 --> 00:49:10.950
- It's unbelievable.
- Yeah?

733
00:49:11.116 --> 00:49:13.576
And you like spending time
with Anna. right?

734
00:49:15.162 --> 00:49:17.662
She might even have
a little thing for you. Heh.

735
00:49:17.873 --> 00:49:19.373
It's cute. Whatever.

736
00:49:19.541 --> 00:49:21.881
I mean. you're a big boy.
you can handle a little attention.

737
00:49:22.044 --> 00:49:25.094
Just congratulate me.

738
00:49:25.672 --> 00:49:27.802
- Jesus. What the...?
- What?

739
00:49:27.966 --> 00:49:31.796
No. congratulations. sweetheart.
Um. I am so proud of you.

740
00:49:33.138 --> 00:49:34.138
I love you.

741
00:49:34.681 --> 00:49:36.311
I'll see you tomorrow.

742
00:49:36.475 --> 00:49:38.475
I love you too. babe.

743
00:49:40.020 --> 00:49:42.020
[♪♪♪]

744
00:50:47.170 --> 00:50:49.420
[SIGHS]

745
00:50:52.092 --> 00:50:54.932
♪ Hypnotised ♪

746
00:50:55.095 --> 00:51:00.385
♪ Even addicted to your grumpy face ♪♪

747
00:51:01.309 --> 00:51:03.519
[DOOR OPENS THEN SLAMS]

748
00:51:04.229 --> 00:51:05.899
JOHN: Anna!

749
00:51:07.482 --> 00:51:10.112
- Hi. John.
- What are you doing?

750
00:51:11.695 --> 00:51:12.945
Look. do you see this?

751
00:51:13.113 --> 00:51:14.873
This is me and Laura.
She is my wife. okay?

752
00:51:15.031 --> 00:51:18.541
This is our home.
Do you not understand that?

753
00:51:19.077 --> 00:51:20.827
I don't wanna have to say anything to her.

754
00:51:21.455 --> 00:51:23.995
Maybe I should go.

755
00:51:24.166 --> 00:51:27.376
No. wait. hold on. No. no. Please. please.

756
00:51:27.544 --> 00:51:29.634
Okay. look.

757
00:51:29.796 --> 00:51:34.256
Maybe... Maybe I said something
to encourage you in all this.

758
00:51:34.426 --> 00:51:36.846
And if I did do that. then I am sorry.

759
00:51:37.012 --> 00:51:38.602
[DOOR OPENS]

760
00:51:38.764 --> 00:51:40.394
Hello!

761
00:51:40.557 --> 00:51:43.557
- Hey.
- Hi.

762
00:51:43.727 --> 00:51:46.227
Didn't wanna wait until tomorrow.
so I grabbed the next flight.

763
00:51:46.396 --> 00:51:49.606
Good. That's... That's good.
Congratulations on everything.

764
00:51:49.775 --> 00:51:51.565
ANNA: Hello. Laura.

765
00:51:54.237 --> 00:51:56.067
[♪♪♪]

766
00:51:56.656 --> 00:51:59.986
Uh. Laura just got a. uh.
promotion at her company.

767
00:52:00.452 --> 00:52:01.452
Oh...

768
00:52:01.661 --> 00:52:04.041
Well. it's only until the baby comes.

769
00:52:04.206 --> 00:52:06.666
- How are you?
- ANNA: Everything is fine.

770
00:52:07.834 --> 00:52:11.924
- Mmm. Welcome home.
- It's good to be back.

771
00:52:12.088 --> 00:52:13.298
It's good to have you back.

772
00:52:17.260 --> 00:52:19.260
