ANNA: I am happy.

833
00:57:20.021 --> 00:57:23.441
I am in control...

834
00:57:23.608 --> 00:57:25.938
...of my life.

835
00:57:26.736 --> 00:57:30.696
I feel the joy...

836
00:57:30.865 --> 00:57:33.905
...of pure love.

837
00:57:41.292 --> 00:57:43.292
[♪♪♪]

838
00:57:47.632 --> 00:57:49.632
[EXHALES SHARPLY THEN CHUCKLES]

839
00:57:51.386 --> 00:57:54.426
LAURA [ON MESSAGE]: Hi. this is Laura
Taylor. Leave a message. and I'll...

840
00:57:57.642 --> 00:57:59.232
I can't hold the room. I'm sorry.

841
00:58:00.145 --> 00:58:01.895
You know what. let's just go ahead and...

842
00:58:02.605 --> 00:58:04.315
- Should we?
- I. um...

843
00:58:04.482 --> 00:58:05.902
- Okay. All right.
- I left a message.

844
00:58:07.110 --> 00:58:09.200
DOCTOR: That's the femur.

845
00:58:10.321 --> 00:58:12.661
It's a boy.

846
00:58:13.366 --> 00:58:14.576
I told you.

847
00:58:15.243 --> 00:58:16.623
DOCTOR: She's right.

848
00:58:16.786 --> 00:58:18.536
That's definitely a boy. Heh.

849
00:58:19.747 --> 00:58:21.207
[PHONE RINGING]

850
00:58:22.667 --> 00:58:25.457
Honey. No. wait.

851
00:58:25.628 --> 00:58:27.378
It's a boy.

852
00:58:28.339 --> 00:58:29.509
- ANNA: It's a boy.
- No. babe...

853
00:58:29.674 --> 00:58:31.974
...just get down here as soon as you can.

854
00:58:33.553 --> 00:58:35.513
That's my son.

855
00:58:37.098 --> 00:58:38.598
I'm looking at my son.

856
00:58:38.766 --> 00:58:41.096
[ANNA & JOHN LAUGHING]

857
00:58:43.855 --> 00:58:46.015
Look at his head.

858
00:58:47.650 --> 00:58:49.530
That's my son.

859
00:58:49.736 --> 00:58:52.106
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

860
00:58:54.282 --> 00:58:55.912
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

861
00:58:57.952 --> 00:59:00.082
[LAURA PANTING]

862
00:59:00.246 --> 00:59:02.496
I'm sorry. I had it in my schedule
as 2:00.

863
00:59:02.665 --> 00:59:06.035
- Maybe you just entered it wrong.
- No. I didn't enter it wrong. I...

864
00:59:06.211 --> 00:59:07.751
Damn it. I know I didn't. I... I...

865
00:59:07.921 --> 00:59:11.591
Someone changed it in my phone!
I know that I put it in right.

866
00:59:11.758 --> 00:59:14.798
I booked my flights around it!
I know that I did! Damn it!

867
00:59:14.969 --> 00:59:17.059
- I... I...
- Laura. Stop it. Please.

868
00:59:18.431 --> 00:59:19.681
Please.

869
00:59:20.600 --> 00:59:21.730
[LAURA SIGHS]

870
00:59:21.893 --> 00:59:26.483
This is the only time
we're ever gonna be able to do this.

871
00:59:26.648 --> 00:59:29.898
It's all right. Just don't worry about it.

872
00:59:32.195 --> 00:59:34.195
[♪♪♪]

873
00:59:38.826 --> 00:59:42.116
Let's just go somewhere.
I don't know. lunch.

874
00:59:45.250 --> 00:59:47.130
I can't.

875
00:59:47.961 --> 00:59:51.011
I left a client at the airport.

876
00:59:52.090 --> 00:59:54.340
I have to go back.

877
01:00:09.983 --> 01:00:10.983
[PHONE RINGS]

878
01:00:11.150 --> 01:00:12.530
WOMAN [OVER PHONE]: Anna Walsh on 2.

879
01:00:12.694 --> 01:00:13.744
JOHN: Hello?

880
01:00:13.903 --> 01:00:17.453
ANNA [OVER PHONE]: I'm so excited. A boy.

881
01:00:17.615 --> 01:00:21.325
I knew it. Let's have lunch today.
To celebrate.

882
01:00:21.536 --> 01:00:23.746
Just you and me. I promise it'll be fun.

883
01:00:23.913 --> 01:00:25.833
- Anna. is there anything actually wrong?
- Why?

884
01:00:25.999 --> 01:00:27.709
Because you shouldn't
be calling me at work.

885
01:00:27.917 --> 01:00:30.457
Okay? I cannot sneak away.
I will not have lunch with you.

886
01:00:30.670 --> 01:00:32.960
I have appointments all afternoon.
Like I said earlier...

887
01:00:33.131 --> 01:00:34.421
[LINE DISCONNECTS]

888
01:00:34.590 --> 01:00:36.590
[♪♪♪]

889
01:00:37.385 --> 01:00:39.175
[PHONE RINGS]

890
01:00:39.971 --> 01:00:43.521
Mr. Taylor's office. Please hold.

891
01:00:44.183 --> 01:00:47.233
- Anna Walsh.
- Tell her I left for the day.

892
01:00:48.021 --> 01:00:49.981
[PHONE RINGING]

893
01:00:56.779 --> 01:00:59.909
- What is it?
- ANNA: Why are you lying to me?

894
01:01:00.491 --> 01:01:02.201
What are you talking about?

895
01:01:02.368 --> 01:01:05.158
I'd never lie to you. John.

896
01:01:06.205 --> 01:01:09.165
I've always told you the truth.

897
01:01:10.043 --> 01:01:12.093
But not you.

898
01:01:12.462 --> 01:01:13.502
Why are you saying that?

899
01:01:13.671 --> 01:01:16.051
Because I'm right here.

900
01:01:21.262 --> 01:01:22.812
Ooh.

901
01:01:24.432 --> 01:01:26.312
[DOOR CLOSES]

902
01:01:28.519 --> 01:01:30.649
This is for you.

903
01:01:31.147 --> 01:01:33.477
A congratulations.

904
01:01:34.442 --> 01:01:36.492
JOHN:
All right. No. we're not gonna do this.

905
01:01:36.652 --> 01:01:39.322
- We're not gonna do this.
- Mm.

906
01:01:39.906 --> 01:01:41.276
Let's do something fun.

907
01:01:42.700 --> 01:01:44.330
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

908
01:01:44.535 --> 01:01:48.785
Nope. We're not doing anything fun.

909
01:01:48.998 --> 01:01:51.578
[♪♪♪]

910
01:01:55.254 --> 01:01:58.304
ANNA: What a surprise.
Laura's working late again!

911
01:01:58.466 --> 01:02:00.296
Why did you think
she would make a good mother?

912
01:02:00.468 --> 01:02:03.008
- Enough!
- We're so different.

913
01:02:03.221 --> 01:02:04.851
She couldn't even stay pregnant.

914
01:02:05.014 --> 01:02:07.024
I wonder if she actually even wanted to.

915
01:02:07.225 --> 01:02:08.635
Are you sure she had miscarriages?

916
01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:11.400
Because you know there are ways
to fake that. right?

917
01:02:11.562 --> 01:02:15.532
- Are you out of your mind?
- You need to be nicer to me. John.

918
01:02:15.691 --> 01:02:18.151
I will leave. The law says I can.

919
01:02:18.319 --> 01:02:22.619
This is my baby. Mike says we can sell it.

920
01:02:24.033 --> 01:02:25.743
[♪♪♪]

921
01:02:26.786 --> 01:02:28.656
- John!
- You know what?

922
01:02:29.789 --> 01:02:31.829
Leave. Go. Get out of the house!

923
01:02:31.999 --> 01:02:34.249
- You don't mean that.
- Oh. yes. I do.

924
01:02:34.460 --> 01:02:37.630
I'll tell Laura everything.
It will kill her. It will break her heart.

925
01:02:37.797 --> 01:02:40.047
But you know what? We'll survive it.

926
01:02:40.383 --> 01:02:43.683
We'll pick up the pieces and move on
because that's what we do.

927
01:02:43.845 --> 01:02:47.135
But what about you? You'll be alone.

928
01:02:47.306 --> 01:02:50.976
You'll be broke.
with a kid that's not even really yours.

929
01:02:51.477 --> 01:02:53.187
So go for it.

930
01:02:53.354 --> 01:02:55.194
Leave.

931
01:03:00.403 --> 01:03:02.953
I just want you.

932
01:03:15.835 --> 01:03:17.165
[DIALLING ON PHONE]

933
01:03:17.795 --> 01:03:19.705
[PHONE RINGING]

934
01:03:22.800 --> 01:03:24.340
[KEYPAD BEEPS]

935
01:03:25.052 --> 01:03:27.432
- White here.
- JOHN: Hey. Roland. it's John.

936
01:03:27.597 --> 01:03:30.927
Hey. what's up? What. the old man
needs another rock looked under?

937
01:03:31.142 --> 01:03:34.102
No. actually. I need a favour.
And it's not business.

938
01:03:34.312 --> 01:03:35.902
- It's personal.
- Sure. John.

939
01:03:36.856 --> 01:03:39.686
There's a guy I'd like you to look into.
His name is Mike Mitchell.

940
01:03:39.859 --> 01:03:41.819
He's Navy. based in Louisiana.

941
01:03:41.986 --> 01:03:44.736
He's been deployed about two months.
Just need a history on him.

942
01:03:44.906 --> 01:03:47.156
Anything you can find would be great.

943
01:03:47.325 --> 01:03:50.235
I'm on it. Anything for you. John.

944
01:03:50.411 --> 01:03:51.911
My man.

945
01:03:55.124 --> 01:03:57.134
[♪♪♪]

946
01:04:00.338 --> 01:04:02.338
[DOOR OPENS]

947
01:04:04.425 --> 01:04:05.465
You wanted to see me?

948
01:04:06.511 --> 01:04:07.551
Have a seat. John.

949
01:04:14.101 --> 01:04:17.561
Look. you know
the firm monitors computer use...

950
01:04:17.730 --> 01:04:19.360
...and e-mail accounts.

951
01:04:19.524 --> 01:04:21.824
The system's set up
to automatically snag...

952
01:04:21.984 --> 01:04:24.824
...certain types of files.
things that could...

953
01:04:25.655 --> 01:04:28.065
...embarrass the company.

954
01:04:35.039 --> 01:04:37.039
[♪♪♪]

955
01:04:47.885 --> 01:04:51.555
Todd recognised her from your party.

956
01:04:51.722 --> 01:04:53.722
She's not your relative. is she?

957
01:04:53.891 --> 01:04:56.891
No. She's our surrogate.

958
01:04:57.061 --> 01:04:58.981
And I don't see
how this is company business.

959
01:04:59.146 --> 01:05:01.436
Anna has been getting
prenatal care from a clinic...

960
01:05:01.607 --> 01:05:03.897
...that happens to be a subsidiary
of Grafton Industries.

961
01:05:04.068 --> 01:05:06.818
She is a patient of the very people...

962
01:05:06.988 --> 01:05:10.118
...we're about to take to court.

963
01:05:10.408 --> 01:05:13.238
That's a big deal. John.

964
01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:15.620
I'm giving the case to Todd.

965
01:05:16.831 --> 01:05:18.831
I hope you understand.

966
01:05:20.376 --> 01:05:22.876
I'm sorry. John. That video got bounced
straight to the old man.

967
01:05:23.045 --> 01:05:25.335
I think I just lost my job.

968
01:05:27.300 --> 01:05:28.880
You ready for things to get worse?

969
01:05:29.093 --> 01:05:30.803
I don't think that's possible.

970
01:05:30.970 --> 01:05:33.510
Remember that guy you asked me
to run a check on? Mitchell?

971
01:05:35.308 --> 01:05:36.848
- Yeah.
- Two years ago...

972
01:05:37.018 --> 01:05:39.438
...he was discharged from the military
for some assaults.

973
01:05:39.604 --> 01:05:41.274
Regular dickhead shit.

974
01:05:41.439 --> 01:05:44.189
But after I saw the video.
I got to thinking about that girl.

975
01:05:44.358 --> 01:05:46.148
- Your girl.
- Yeah. and...?

976
01:05:46.319 --> 01:05:48.399
Well. her real name isn't Walsh.

977
01:05:48.696 --> 01:05:51.446
She got married at 19 in Little Rock.

978
01:05:51.616 --> 01:05:54.156
Before that. she was Anna Devost.

979
01:05:54.952 --> 01:05:58.412
Which is why the surrogate agency
missed this.

980
01:05:58.581 --> 01:06:01.751
Marijuana. A DUI.

981
01:06:01.917 --> 01:06:03.877
Nothing horrible. really.

982
01:06:04.045 --> 01:06:06.755
But not exactly the picture of innocence.

983
01:06:06.922 --> 01:06:10.342
So I dug a little deeper.

984
01:06:10.509 --> 01:06:12.349
She was born in Memphis.

985
01:06:12.511 --> 01:06:14.851
Her parents died when she was 3.

986
01:06:15.014 --> 01:06:17.604
Raised by foster parents.

987
01:06:17.767 --> 01:06:20.647
She lived with them for 12 years.

988
01:06:22.688 --> 01:06:25.568
Now. this took some work to get to.

989
01:06:25.733 --> 01:06:28.033
When she was 16.
she attacks her foster dad...

990
01:06:28.194 --> 01:06:30.204
...with a pair of scissors.

991
01:06:30.363 --> 01:06:32.283
Killed him.

992
01:06:32.448 --> 01:06:34.488
Seems she had a reason.

993
01:06:34.659 --> 01:06:37.869
The guy was sexually abusing her.

994
01:06:39.789 --> 01:06:41.829
State takes over...

995
01:06:41.999 --> 01:06:44.249
...puts her in psych.

996
01:06:47.713 --> 01:06:49.883
She's a minor. so the records are sealed.

997
01:06:50.049 --> 01:06:54.049
But when she turns 18.
she walks out and is gone.

998
01:06:54.345 --> 01:06:56.715
She's dangerous. John.

999
01:06:56.889 --> 01:06:59.519
WOMAN: You're right where you should be.

1000
01:06:59.684 --> 01:07:03.024
And you slowly begin
to reawaken yourself...

1001
01:07:03.187 --> 01:07:06.017
...with small movements.

1002
01:07:06.190 --> 01:07:08.780
You appreciate your mind and your body...

1003
01:07:08.943 --> 01:07:12.073
...for the accomplishments of this lesson.

1004
01:07:14.782 --> 01:07:16.082
[WOMEN LAUGHING]

1005
01:07:16.242 --> 01:07:19.372
LAURA: Aw. thank you so much.

1006
01:07:19.537 --> 01:07:21.617
- Thank you.
- JOHN'S MOTHER: Okay. it's my turn.

1007
01:07:23.833 --> 01:07:26.173
This was John's great-grandmother's...

1008
01:07:26.335 --> 01:07:29.955
- WOMAN 1: Oh...
- ...and then my mother and then mine.

1009
01:07:30.131 --> 01:07:31.511
I always wanted you to have it.

1010
01:07:31.674 --> 01:07:34.184
Oh... John told me about this.

1011
01:07:40.307 --> 01:07:43.017
JOHN'S MOTHER: Isn't it lovely?

1012
01:07:43.477 --> 01:07:45.187
- WOMEN: Oh...
- WOMAN 2: Oh. that's so cute.

1013
01:07:47.022 --> 01:07:48.362
[PLAYING "ROCK-A-BYE BABY" SLOWLY]

1014
01:07:48.524 --> 01:07:50.484
[LAUGHS]

1015
01:07:52.069 --> 01:07:54.069
[SIGHS]

1016
01:07:56.949 --> 01:07:59.079
LAURA: Thank you.

1017
01:08:00.202 --> 01:08:02.002
[WATER DRIPPING]

1018
01:08:02.163 --> 01:08:04.123
[♪♪♪]

1019
01:08:28.063 --> 01:08:32.993
♪ Rock-a-bye. baby ♪

1020
01:08:34.695 --> 01:08:38.315
♪ In the tree top ♪

1021
01:08:40.201 --> 01:08:44.161
♪ When the wind blows ♪

1022
01:08:45.372 --> 01:08:49.292
♪ The cradle will rock ♪

1023
01:08:52.630 --> 01:08:57.050
♪ When the bough breaks ♪

1024
01:08:58.511 --> 01:09:04.021
♪ The cradle will fall ♪

1025
01:09:07.603 --> 01:09:16.783
♪ And down will come baby ♪

1026
